    "Femenino",
    "Neutro"
   ]
  },
  {
   "tipo": "explicacion",
   "titulo": "Me, you, us and you",
   "texto": [
    "**Mein** (mi) and **dein** (tu) change as «ein»: **mein Vater**, **meine Mutter**, **meine Eltern** (plural). **Unser** (our) and **euer** (your) follow the same pattern: **unser Bruder**, **unsere Schwester**, **unsere Eltern**; **euer Vater**, **eure Mutter**. The **euer** form loses a «e» by adding the termination: **eure**."
   ]
  },
